ampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466392#post1466392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Dam there goes one of the Money Vampire Clans, One Two left, what I have left is the Crown Clan and the Blue Bloods, <br /> <br /> LW</div> </div> </div> </div>The Giovanni are still rich, they just have new cousins and in-laws, in a sense, working with them and telling them what to do. Which is a bit like the experience of some of the secondary families with the Giovanni themselves.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T06:35:49-07:00","id":1466455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Spencer from The Hills</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466447#post1466447\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Giovanni are still rich, they just have new cousins and in-laws, in a sense, working with them and telling them what to do. Which is a bit like the experience of some of the secondary families with the Giovanni themselves.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I'd argue they are probably more powerful than they have ever been.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27090-jonny","name":"Jonny","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"60"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T13:57:41-07:00","id":1466511,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466267#post1466267\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think canonically they pretty much did exactly this, except they didn't consider the Giovanni Sub-Families &quot;True&quot; Giovanni and on the hit list.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tell that to the Pisanobs. They got gutted badly by the Harbingers to the point of near extinction until the head of their family, Pochtli offered himself up to them to spare what was left of his family.<br /> <br /> Which actually would make sense. It's rumored that Pochtli was a Cappadocian and a Premascine which would explain the Harbingers hatred for him and his family. To me it never made much sense why the Harbingers were so hell-bent on killing the Giovanni as they were supposed to be survivors of the Feast of Folly, something that happened long before Augustus was even born. If anything, they should <i><b>HATE</b></i> their fellow Cappadocians and their anger at the Giovanni should solely be because the Giovanni stole their vengeance from them. But on the other hand, Pochtli and by extent his Childer being Cappadocians would make them targets, especially if Pochtli was around before the Feast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466429#post1466429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally i just figured its because cappadocious and most of the methusulahs are dead.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it's ultimately unclear why they're immune to the Beckoning. The Ritual is one suggestion thrown out. Another is as you say, Cappadocious and much of their Methuselahs are dead and gone.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466437#post1466437\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, with the Caveat that Cappadocius may still be active even then, as a Wraith or an \u00dcbber-Wraith.</div> </div> </div> </div>He was a Wraith but the Fourth or Fifth Great Maelstrom got him and he became a Spectre, a particularly insane one. Not that he had a lot of sanity to begin with.<br /> <br /> As for him being still active, it's possible but currently unknown. Though with him no longer being a vampire, I would imagine that his pull over his line's Blood is rather limited.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:32:41-07:00","id":1466567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AkatsukiLeader13</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466511#post1466511\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He was a Wraith but the Fourth or Fifth Great Maelstrom got him and he became a Spectre, a particularly insane one. Not that he had a lot of sanity to begin with.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember this, not that it really matters a lot.<br /> <br /> His plan was to die so he could eat God. Otherwise he never had much of an interest in Kindred society anyway and just wanted to study death. I don't see him interacting with the rest of the clan in any meaningful way from now on, and if he does it will be in a way that makes his status as their Ante irrelevant.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:35:30-07:00","id":1466568,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jonny</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466455#post1466455\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue they are probably more powerful than they have ever been.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. The Giovanni still have their wealth. That didn't really vanish. They just added all of the necromantic knowledge of the Harbringers, Samedi, Cappadocians, Nagaraja, etc. Plus the clan is no longer bound to Augustus' goal of Eternal Night so there's a lot more freedom and options. Many of the older elders are dead and the newer elders generally aren't as interested in things like money or the modern world, so the Giovanni who survived (most of them younger ones whose power was limited in the old family) also have more freedom and power now. <br /> <br /> It's mostly a win-win for everyone except for Augustus and his more immediate family members.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-03T18:40:33-07:00","id":1466569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466567#post1466567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't remember this, not that it really matters a lot.<br /> <br /> His plan was to die so he could eat God. Otherwise he never had much of an interest in Kindred society anyway and just wanted to study death. I don't see him interacting with the rest of the clan in any meaningful way from now on, and if he does it will be in a way that makes his status as their Ante irrelevant.</div> </div> </div> </div>This was all in Giovanni Chronicles. Cappadocius turned into a Spectre during one of the Maelstroms of the underworld and his plans to eat God were put on hold by his desire for revenge against the Giovanni and the Ventrue. He shows up at the end and the 4th book and the PCs (or rather the PCs from the first 3 games) put him to rest using a ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T16:32:59-07:00","id":1466993,"title":"","content":"Just to clarify a few things:<br /> <br /> -The Giovanni are still the most populous bloodline in the Hecata. They also have retained their nominal power as they control the council that rules the clan. <br /> -Not all Giovanni elders were killed/sacrificed. Many survived because they were not close to Augustus.<br /> -the Capuchin (all 3 of them) is the real power behind the throne inside the Hecata.<br /> -No one knows what happened to Augustus. He might still be around in hiding or he might be dead, it\u2019s not specified and it\u2019s on purpose as having Augustus coming back with vengeance is a good story hook.<br /> -The harbingers of skulls are said to be a bloodline of assassins from the cappadocians ranks sacrificed during the Feast of Folly. Apparently they wanted revenge against the Giovanni because they killed Cappadocius stealing their chance to do the same (silly, I know, but at least the HoS are supposed to be deranged after spending centuries in the shadowlands surviving on the essence of wraiths)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T20:52:32-07:00","id":1467010,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Haquim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1466993#post1466993\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just to clarify a few things:<br /> -The harbingers of skulls are said to be a bloodline of assassins from the cappadocians ranks sacrificed during the Feast of Folly. Apparently they wanted revenge against the Giovanni because they killed Cappadocius stealing their chance to do the same (silly, I know, but at least the HoS are supposed to be deranged after spending centuries in the shadowlands surviving on the essence of wraiths)</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually V20 Lore of the Bloodlines established that. Well mostly. The Feast of Folly was always presented as a purge of those of the Clan that weren't Christians and Scholars. This just confirmed that Harbingers wing were indeed the muscle, spies and killers of the Clan rather than just an assortment of those that didn't fit into role Cappadocius wanted to forge the Clan into. Or possibly to prevent there being enough fighters within the Clan to stop the purges if he was indeed thinking that far ahead.<br /> <br /> As for their hatred for the Giovanni, it's complicated and varies between Harbingers. Some hate them because they stole their chance at vengeance on Cappadocius. Others because they view Augustus and the purges the Giovanni conducted as part of Cappadocius' plot and wish to destroy them because of that. A few believe that Augustus unknowningly carries one of three fragments of Cappadocius' soul. The other two pieces likely being his wraith/spectre and the True Vessel. So killing him is destroying Cappadocius. And of course, some are just a bit nuts.<br /> <br /> Speaking of LotB, I had forgotten but it does actually mention something what would be come to play in V5, the Harbingers reaching out to potential allies within the Giovanni. Though amusingly, they include among those allies the Pisanobs. I guess that didn't work out for them.<br /> <br /> Or the Harbingers were simply using their old skills as spies and assassins again by getting close to their targets.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T20:56:07-07:00","id":1467011,"title":"","content":"I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore. It seems like a thing all Antediluvians would do from time to time. I mean, purge your Clan of the stragglers is just good business. Instead, now it's like this unprecedented thing that left deep lasting scars on the Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I prefer the Feast of Folly got rid of the losers of the Cappadocians and not some genius misunderstood bloodline.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 11-06-2021, 11:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-06T21:28:49-07:00","id":1467012,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467011#post1467011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore. It seems like a thing all Antediluvians would do from time to time. I mean, purge your Clan of the stragglers is just good business. Instead, now it's like this unprecedented thing that left deep lasting scars on the Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I prefer the Feast of Folly got rid of the losers of the Cappadocians and not some genius misunderstood bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>With the Feast I think it's a number of factors involved as to why it's so notable. The first being that it spawned a Bloodline and much of the talk of the Feast is through their eyes so for them it's rather... <i>important</i>. And because it effectively created the Bloodline it is important lore-wise. Second, I think even in-universe the Feast is looked at as a factor that contributed to the purge of the Cappadocians. Not only did it removing Cappadocians that could have been able to protect their more scholarly kin but some were operating in roles that could detected and prevented it.<br /> <br /> Most importantly, the Feast of Folly has become part of Cappadocius' mad schemes for Godhood, that he sacrificed his Clan twice over in some insane quest to become God. It's part of his madness, that madness that can only strike one that has lived so long and possesses so much power yet craves more.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:04:44-07:00","id":1467022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467011#post1467011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore. It seems like a thing all Antediluvians would do from time to time. I mean, purge your Clan of the stragglers is just good business. Instead, now it's like this unprecedented thing that left deep lasting scars on the Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I prefer the Feast of Folly got rid of the losers of the Cappadocians and not some genius misunderstood bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we go with a Cyclical Gehenna, the Feast of Folly is also an awesome blueprint.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:16:35-07:00","id":1467023,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467011#post1467011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore. It seems like a thing all Antediluvians would do from time to time. I mean, purge your Clan of the stragglers is just good business. Instead, now it's like this unprecedented thing that left deep lasting scars on the Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I prefer the Feast of Folly got rid of the losers of the Cappadocians and not some genius misunderstood bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, it was literally a big deal from the get-go. It was always supposed to be a big deal and it was one of the milestones that led to the Giovanni usurping the Cappadocians. And it would leave deep scars, especially because Cappadocius was one of the more 'present' Antediluvians, and his clan had a relationship with him at the time.<br /> <br /> It's like saying the Week of Nightmares shouldn't be important to the Ravnos, because all Antediluvians cull their childer. Of course these things matter to the clan that experiences them (note also how Xavier fled the Camarilla because he realised his Antediluvian has melded with the earth's core, for instance; or how some Lasombra reacted when they realised their Antediluvian was still alive).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T01:29:22-08:00","id":1467025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467011#post1467011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some key aspects to understand the Feast of Folly:<br /> <br /> 1 - The Cappadocian was the biggest clan at the time. Affecting any percentage of them is a bigger thing than affecting the same percentage anywhere else;<br /> <br /> 2 - It is also a very organized clan for the time, but also very quiet. Even if irregular purges were a thing in other clans, the Feast <b>was</b> unprecedented for them. This story is about their perception, so that's what matters;<br /> <br /> 3 - About half the attendees are reported as affected. This' a big proportion for any purge, so pretty much an unprecedented purge when we combine those first 3 factors;<br /> <br /> 4 - Cappadocius called the clan to their seat of power and most sacred place at the time, so it isn't just a culling happening at a random place. And the place itself is lost to the clan as it is turned into a prison. This adds a lot of significance to the fact by itself;<br /> <br /> 5 - No killing is reported before the closing. That means that instead of &quot;simply&quot; a purge what happened was that a huge amount of Kindred for the time got themselves entombed alive in a sacred labyrinth, left to their own devices.<br /> <br /> But what really makes the event relevant is it causing splits in the clan that had no splits before. It isn't a sign of Gehenna or anything, but the event in their history that defines the origins of Infitiores and Harbingers, maybe more. It is the earliest schism in the Cappadocian, and if nothing else is exquisitely executed.<br /> <br /> You shouldn't claim it got rid of losers, though, as this was not quite the intent. No one involved describes the Feast as that. Cappadocius had an arcane set of requirements related mainly to their ability as researchers, which gives credence to <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar420_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"420\" data-vbnamecard=\"420\">AkatsukiLeader13</a>'s affirmation, at the very least the Feast victimized members whose main assets were to give support to the clan outside doing research, including soldiers, assassins and spies. So at the very least the victims were &quot;<i>losers</i>&quot; only as defined by a very unhinged guy.<br /> <br /> Maybe there was other reasons behind the decisions or the entire endeavor. It is a very strange occurrence, an extremely specific way to get rid of excess baggage when most Ancients are far more straightforward about it. Even if not, the result is a bloodline entirely comprised of elders or, more probably, Methuselah with an extremely close relation to the Underworld.<br /> <br /> Just to have a notion of the numbers: it's reported only among attendees more than <b>12 thousand</b> Cappadocians. By all accounts this should be more than the entire Kindred population at the time. If you go by the set standard of 1:100k Kindred-to-Human ratio, they would need a population of around 1.2 <i>billion</i> humans. At the time of Augustus' Embrace, an unspecified amount of time after the Feast, the entire world population is estimated at 310 <i>millions</i>, less than 26 thousand mortals in the entire world for every Cappadocian that just appeared at the Feast.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T03:08:49-08:00","id":1467035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467011#post1467011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I feel like the Feast of Folly has been incredibly overstated in the lore. It seems like a thing all Antediluvians would do from time to time. I mean, purge your Clan of the stragglers is just good business. Instead, now it's like this unprecedented thing that left deep lasting scars on the Clan.<br /> <br /> Mind you, I prefer the Feast of Folly got rid of the losers of the Cappadocians and not some genius misunderstood bloodline.</div> </div> </div> </div>Worth remembering that (in the Dark Ages timeline) the Feast of Folly happened within fairly recent (undead) memory, likely only around 100-200 years before the Dark Ages setting). The vast majority of the Antediluvians were in topor by that point or hadn't been seen in centuries or longer. Cappadocius goes and and publicly murders half of his clan. If Antedulivans had been doing things like that, those accounts were very apocryphal and forgotten. Even outside of Dark Ages, looking at the general timeline, the Feast of Folly was the last major, public action taken by an Antediluvian until Ravnos woke up. It was a pretty major thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 11-07-2021, 06:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T04:18:13-08:00","id":1467038,"title":"","content":"The inordinate focus on the Feast of Folly is just a symptom of an issue that has plagued the Cappadocian concept from the beginning: an excessive focus on the clan founder and metaplot developments at the expense of player-facing material about the clan. Who thought that giving a clan of reclusive scholars and mystics the most active, the most meddling, the most micromanaging founder to have ever unlived was a good idea? Achilli's <i>Clanbook: Cappadocian</i> is more interested in the personal history and psychology of Cappadocius than in the history and evolution of the clan. Cappadocius is supposed to be a genuine Antediluvian blood god from prehistoric times, yet we know more about his personality, his wacky shenanigans, and his kooky plans than about the goings-on of the youngest clan founders, Tremere and Augustus Giovanni. Nothing could kill all sense of mystery about the Antediluvians more effectively.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1190,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","user":"Elphilm","date":". 11-07-2021, 07:24 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1190-elphilm","name":"Elphilm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1190_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"763"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:14:43-08:00","id":1467055,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467038#post1467038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inordinate focus on the Feast of Folly is just a symptom of an issue that has plagued the Cappadocian concept from the beginning: an excessive focus on the clan founder and metaplot developments at the expense of player-facing material about the clan.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's very much true. From a Doylist perspective the FoF is pretty much a symptom of the general problem with the Cappadocian being a Plot Device first, the Ante's background second, and a clan as a far third.<br /> <br /> Yet I wouldn't say we have less on Cappadocius than we have on Tremere, but for a single reason: for Tremere we have <i>Ars Magica</i>'s lore before even any VtM lore on him, and because of this, also some lore in Mage books.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T09:21:40-08:00","id":1467056,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467055#post1467055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's very much true. From a Doylist perspective the FoF is pretty much a symptom of the general problem with the Cappadocian being a Plot Device first, the Ante's background second, and a clan as a far third.<br /> <br /> Yet I wouldn't say we have less on Cappadocius than we have on Tremere, but for a single reason: for Tremere we have <i>Ars Magica</i>'s lore before even any VtM lore on him, and because of this, also some lore in Mage books.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd actually say Set is the most developed Antediluvian because we have mythology, his family issues, the fact he's a redhead, and also his obsessive number of Embracing hot priestesses which implies something about his priorities.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-07T10:04:02-08:00","id":1467064,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467056#post1467056\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd actually say Set is the most developed Antediluvian because we have mythology, his family issues, the fact he's a redhead, and also his obsessive number of Embracing hot priestesses which implies something about his priorities.</div> </div> </div> </div>True, but we actually have very little being told <b><i>objectively</i></b> about Set. We do have a lot of info, but most of this info is from extremely unreliable sources, things like old texts that are translations of older texts that are re-telling of older oral traditions that are supposed to come from Isis.<br /> <br /> Like it or not, Set is mostly known through stories told by people that lived way after the time of the events. His actual contemporaries either don't tell a lot, didn't lived to talk directly (as many weren't vampires or mummies), or are somehow unreliable (weren't there in person, have a lot of conflict of interest, or have been unable to distinguish memory from delirium for the past thousand years at least).<br /> <br /> With Cappadocius and Tremere we have a number of considerably more reliable sources, up to and including information that's confirmed OoC to be canon. As much as I don't think this is a good take on the matter, it's still canon. Most of Set's stuff is presented only as legend even when treated as almost certainly true.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-08T11:12:11-08:00","id":1467186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elphilm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1466122-v5-clan-giovanni?p=1467038#post1467038\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The inordinate focus on the Feast of Folly is just a symptom of an issue that has plagued the Cappadocian concept from the beginning: an excessive focus on the clan founder and metaplot developments at the expense of player-facing material about the clan. Who thought that giving a clan of reclusive scholars and mystics the most active, the most meddling, the most micromanaging founder to have ever unlived was a good idea? Achilli's <i>Clanbook: Cappadocian</i> is more interested in the personal history and psychology of Cappadocius than in the history and evolution of the clan. Cappadocius is supposed to be a genuine Antediluvian blood god from prehistoric times, yet we know more about his personality, his wacky shenanigans, and his kooky plans than about the goings-on of the youngest clan founders, Tremere and Augustus Giovanni. Nothing could kill all sense of mystery about the Antediluvians more effectively.</div> </div> </div> </div>True but the original da corebook does a really good job of writing the clan up so the clanbook isn't particulary neccisary.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}